export const REGISTER_DOC = "# Data-processing register\n\nVersion: 2026-10-03\n\nWhich systems hold or process personal data for Partners in Biz and its clients, what they get, where they are, how long they keep it, and whether an agreement (a data-processing agreement, \"operator agreement\" under POPIA section 21) is on file. The CRM seeds this table from this file (read-only: nothing in the plugin edits a row; to change one, edit this file and ship it).\n\nHow to read the columns:\n\n- **region**: where the data sits. POPIA section 72 limits sending personal data out of South Africa unless the receiver is bound by comparable rules, the person agrees, or a contract needs it.\n- **agreement**: `on file` only when the agreement was seen and kept. `unverified` means nobody has checked: it is a to-do, not a yes.\n- **sensitive clients**: the first word is the rule the Cockpit and Jev routing read. `cleared` means a client flagged sensitive may have its data handled there. `not cleared` means it must not. `conditional` means only with the stated condition. Until an agreement is on file the answer for an outside processor is `not cleared`.\n- Nothing here is legal advice; the owner confirms each `unverified` line.\n\n<!-- register:start -->\n| id | name | role | purpose | data | region | retention | agreement | safeguards | sensitive clients | owner action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| hetzner | Hetzner (the Paperclip server) | Hosting (operator) | Runs Paperclip, its Postgres database, the plugins, Hermes and the preview service | all CRM records, contacts, client leads, issues and comments, mail copies, ledger, agent run logs | EU (Hetzner Online; the data centre is in Finland or Germany, which one is unverified) | Until we delete it; nightly backups kept per the backup policy | unverified | Disk and off-site backups are encrypted (age); only Peet holds the key; access by SSH keys | cleared (our own server; no third party reads the data) | Confirm the data centre and accept Hetzner's data-processing agreement in the Hetzner console; keep a copy |\n| anthropic | Anthropic (Claude) | AI model provider (operator) | Runs the Claude agents (claude_local): they read issue text, CRM records, client briefs and emails to do the work | whatever is in an agent's task: contact names, emails, messages, client business details, draft emails | United States (exact location unverified) | Per Anthropic's terms for the plan in use (unverified which applies) | unverified | Agents are told never to put secrets or credentials in prompts; run logs stay on our server | not cleared (until the agreement and retention terms are confirmed) | Check which Anthropic terms cover our use (subscription or API), whether a data-processing addendum applies and how long prompts are kept; record the answer here |\n| hermes-nous | Nous Research and DeepSeek (through Hermes) | AI model provider (operator) | Runs the Hermes agents (CRM Data Steward, Inbound Qualifier, Sales Lead, SEO Specialist, Plan Critic, Wiki Maintainer) on the nous provider with a DeepSeek model | the same as any agent task: CRM text, lead messages, site content | unverified (the inference host and its country are not documented) | unverified | unverified | None beyond our own prompts; no contract known | not cleared | Find out where the nous portal runs the model and under what terms; until then keep sensitive clients off Hermes agents |\n| typesafe | TypeSafe AI (Jev) | Decision-model provider (operator) | Sorts replies, scores leads and triages mail (short text in, a label out) | email subject and snippet, lead descriptions, reply text | unverified | Zero data retention is an enterprise-plan feature; otherwise unverified | unverified | The CRM sends the least text it can; no key, no call (without a key the built-in rules run) | not cleared (use Laya on our own server for these clients once it exists) | Ask TypeSafe for their data terms, or plan Laya on the VPS for sensitive clients |\n| google | Google (Gmail, Drive, Search Console, Analytics) | Mail, files and search data (operator) | The Mailbox reads and sends Gmail; Drive holds shared files; SEO reads Search Console and Analytics | all email to and from partnersinbiz.online, attachments, search performance of client sites | Global (Google chooses the data centre) | Until deleted from the account | unverified (Google Workspace data-processing amendment, if we are a Workspace customer) | OAuth with least access; tokens held as Paperclip secrets | conditional (mail of a sensitive client is handled only in a mailbox the client agreed to) | Confirm whether the account is Google Workspace and accept the data-processing amendment in the admin console |\n| cloudflare-r2 | Cloudflare R2 | Object storage (operator) | Stores media for Social and the encrypted nightly off-site backup | images, videos, documents clients send us; the backup bundle (encrypted before upload) | unverified (the bucket location was never recorded) | Backups follow the retention policy; media until deleted | unverified (Cloudflare's data-processing addendum is part of its customer terms) | The backup is age-encrypted before it leaves the server; media is not | conditional (a client's media may be stored here only if the client agreed; the backup is encrypted) | Record the bucket's jurisdiction and confirm the Cloudflare data-processing addendum |\n| resend | Resend | Email delivery provider (operator) | Planned sender for marketing email; the domain already has its DKIM selector; the live sender today is Gmail | recipient address, name, message | United States (unverified) | Per Resend's terms | unverified | No mail goes through it until it is switched on in Campaigns | not cleared | Decide whether Resend will be used; if so accept its data-processing agreement first |\n| github | GitHub | Code hosting (operator) | Hosts the client and Partners in Biz repositories; agents push branches and open pull requests | source code, issue and pull request text, sometimes personal data in commits or fixtures | United States | Until deleted | unverified (GitHub's data-protection agreement is part of its terms) | Fine-grained token, repo-scoped; secrets are not committed (checked by a guard) | conditional (a sensitive client's code goes to a private repo; never personal data in a commit) | Confirm the GitHub data-protection agreement for the organisation |\n| vercel | Vercel | Web hosting (operator) | Hosts partnersinbiz.online and several client websites and their previews | the websites' content, form submissions that pass through them, environment settings | Global with a United States default (the region per project is unverified) | Per project | unverified | Previews sit behind login where the plan allows; environment values are secrets | conditional (a sensitive client's site is hosted in a region the client accepted) | Confirm Vercel's data-processing agreement and each project's region |\n| firebase | Firebase (Google Cloud) | App backend (operator) | The older Partners in Biz platform and some client apps keep their users and data in Firebase | app users, contact and lead records of the older platform | unverified (the Firestore location differs per project) | Until deleted | unverified (the Google Cloud data-processing terms) | Service accounts held as secrets | conditional (only in a project whose region the client accepted) | List each Firebase project, its region and which client it serves |\n| paperclip-telemetry | Paperclip (upstream telemetry) | Product telemetry (operator) | The Paperclip server can report usage to its makers | unverified (what is sent is not documented here) | unverified | unverified | unverified | Telemetry is switched on by default in the version we run | not cleared | Read what Paperclip sends and switch it off if it carries anything personal |\n| payment-providers | Payment providers (PayFast, Stripe) | Payments (separate responsible party) | Billing can take card payments once a provider's keys are saved; today invoices are paid by EFT | payer name, email and the payment reference; card numbers never reach us | South Africa (PayFast) and United States (Stripe) | Per the provider | not applicable until switched on | Disabled until the owner saves keys; the provider holds the card data | not cleared (until switched on and reviewed) | Review each provider's terms before saving keys |\n<!-- register:end -->\n";
